A||N||1||fierovette||Figure this out, Oil Pressure.||||5||
Z||000000||fierovette||08-22-2001||03:57 PM||||For many years the gauge pegged past Max. Last mounth I replaced the sender, that seemed to do it, it read at 50ish, idle at 35/40. I took the long way home from Williamsburg, and everyday the gauge was reading lower and lower everyday. When we got home, after 4 days, the oil pressure was at 35 all the time, even at idle. Today going out it was right above the red(20?)Still does not move, same at idle or doing 50.Is it new sender time again, or is it the gauge this time. The engine sounds OK. No rapping or knocking, looking for a simple test to fix the oil pressure gague once and for all.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||08-22-2001||05:00 PM||||You may want to get a manual oil pressure guage to check it out.  Bad sending units, from my experience (5X) always pegged the guage.  Bad oil pump or some other problem i.e. bad guage, would cause low readings.  You need to verify accuracy of the guage.<P>The plus is no engine noises, but if or when they start, it may be too late.||||reg||1
